  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jitesh Ashok Kurliye vs The Police Inspector, Jinsi Police ... on 10 January, 2020 Author: R. G. Avachat Bench: R. G. Avachat 1 aba-1479-19.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1479 Of 2019 Jitesh Ashok Kurliye ... Applicant Versus The Police Inspector, Jinsi Police Station, Tq. & Dist. Aurangabad ... Respondent .... Mr. S. S. Chapalgaonkar, Advocate for applicant. Mr. S. D. Ghayal, App for respondent. .... Coram : R. G. Avachat, J. Dated : 10th January, 2020 Per Court :- .",
    "facts": "The applicant claims to have an apprehension of being arrested in connection with Crime No.0316/2019, registered at Jinsi Police Station, Aurangabad, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 273, 328 read with Section 34 of the Indian Penal Code and under Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. It is alleged in the FIR that an information was received that some persons are selling Gutkha and Pan Masala at Baijipura, Sanjaynagar, Aurangabad. Some of the police officials, therefore, kept a watch in that area. It was found that one Prabhu Makariye and Jitesh Kurliye (applicant) came on two Activa scooter, carrying fully loaded three gunny bags on each Activa scooter. They were, therefore, intercepted and search was made. It was found that the gunny bags contained the packets of Hira Pan Masala. The same came to be seized, since, sale, store and transportation of Gutkha and Pan Masala is prohibited in the State of Maharashtra. FIR, then came to be lodged for the aforesaid offences. 3. I have already observed that Section 328 of Indian Penal Code is not applicable in case of storing, sale or transporting contraband articles, namely, Gutkha, Pan Masala, Tobacco etc. Rest of the offences are bailable one.",
